#uuid "258b6df0-7357-5812-b3c8-874cafe1e994" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317069/field-4/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-317069/field-4/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317069" :question/id #uuid "b6af6fab-87f4-501e-a8f1-9837b9d39287" :question/math-academy-id "q-317069" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 5y+9x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317069/field-1" "q-317069/field-2" "q-317069/field-3" "q-317069/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
